From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:47:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 383/384] Input: matrix_keypad: keep scanning while a key is
 held

In row interrupt mode, a key held between scans keeps its row asserted.
A second key in the same row then raises no row interrupt and is not
scanned. On the Gemini PDA keyboard, an AW9523 matrix with row
interrupts, Left Shift held before Z went unreported because both are
in row 3. Ctrl and Alt, both in row 4, behaved the same. Both
combinations work in polling mode.

When held-poll-interval is set and any key is held after a scan, keep
the row interrupts disabled and the columns inactive. Schedule the next
scan after that interval. Once a scan finds every key released, drive
the columns and enable the row interrupts as before. A stopped device
always takes the normal path, so stop and start keep the disable depth
balanced.

Compile-tested only; not yet run on hardware.
---
 drivers/input/keyboard/matrix_keypad.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/matrix_keypad.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/matrix_keypad.c
index 4635ad7f3..1407013fc 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/matrix_keypad.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/matrix_keypad.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ struct matrix_keypad {
 	/* key debounce interval in milli-second */
 	unsigned int debounce_ms;
 	unsigned int poll_interval_ms;
+	unsigned int held_poll_ms;
 	bool drive_inactive_cols;
 	bool needs_ghost_filter;
 
@@ -166,6 +167,7 @@ static void matrix_keypad_scan(struct work_struct *work)
 	uint32_t new_state[MATRIX_MAX_COLS];
 	int row, col, code;
 	u32 init_row_state, new_row_state;
+	u32 held = 0;
 	int err = 0;
 
 	/* read initial row state to detect changes between scan */
@@ -244,6 +246,24 @@ static void matrix_keypad_scan(struct work_struct *work)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A held key keeps its row asserted, so a second key in the same row
+	 * raises no row interrupt. While any key is held, keep the row
+	 * interrupts off and scan again after the held-key interval.
+	 */
+	for (col = 0; col < keypad->num_col_gpios; col++)
+		held |= new_state[col] | keypad->last_key_state[col];
+
+	if (held && keypad->held_poll_ms) {
+		scoped_guard(spinlock_irq, &keypad->lock) {
+			if (!keypad->stopped) {
+				schedule_delayed_work(&keypad->work,
+						      msecs_to_jiffies(keypad->held_poll_ms));
+				return;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	activate_all_cols(keypad, true);
 
 	/* Enable IRQs again */
@@ -527,6 +547,8 @@ static int matrix_keypad_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 				 &keypad->all_cols_on_delay_us);
 	device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "poll-interval",
 				 &keypad->poll_interval_ms);
+	device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "held-poll-interval",
+				 &keypad->held_poll_ms);
 	keypad->needs_ghost_filter =
 		device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev, "needs-ghost-filter");
 
